Subject: [PATCH] jasmine-j0129: "gpu hang" on the command port dumps a GPU that stopped without an SMMU fault

The Maps pinch freeze leaves a job pending forever with no SMMU fault, so the
j0125 dump never runs. "gpu hang" copies RBBM/CP status, the IB1/IB2 fetch
pointers and 64 dwords around each, the ring around CP_RB_RPTR, and the last 16
jobs into a static snapshot under gpu_lock, then prints after dropping it. It
never resumes or resets a wedged GPU, reads no register while GX is collapsed,
reads GPU memory only through a valid PTE whose physical page this driver was
given, and prints at most about 60 lines. The A5xx offsets are now right
(CP_HW_FAULT 0x0b1a, CP_INTERRUPT_STATUS 0x0b18, CP_PROTECT_STATUS 0x0b1c);
0x0821/0x0823/0x0824 are the CP ROQ/MEQ debug address/data registers and the
MEQ data port has side effects. Diagnostic only: nothing changes unless the
command is sent.

